# moonshots.phext — the Moonshot registry

Will's ruling (PH: Revenue, 2026-11-22 08:06 CST, EE 70):
"number Moonshots monotonically from inception. Track them in
moonshots.phext and keep them in exo-plan."

His framing, verbatim: "we've not been planning ahead or
executing to a design until this wavelet (W4)" — Wavelet 4
(2026-11-22–28) is where planned, to-a-design execution
begins. The eleven moonshots below predate it as pushes,
not plans.

## WIP limit and the migration gate

Will's question (2026-11-22 08:09 CST): "what's needed to
migrate Moonshots to shipped? Keep a Moonshots wip limit
of 10."

WIP LIMIT: at most 10 moonshots in WIP at any time.
A moonshot migrates to shipped.phext (the companion register,
same exo-plan home) when ALL of these stand:
(a) its stated completion bar is met — bars are W4 design
    work; a moonshot without a stated bar cannot migrate,
    because shipped would be unverifiable;
(b) the receipts stand on their own — durable artifacts that
    stand on their own (Will's definition): ship commits,
    hashes, live verifications;
(c) an audit verdict of READY, on the QC-gate pattern —
    ietf.phext's audit chain is the exemplar;
(c') a QC signoff, AND
(c") the project's behavior documented on docs.phext.io —
    the shipped rule (Will, 2026-11-22 08:36 CST): "before
    projects can be considered shipped, they must have a
    QC signoff and documented behavior on docs.phext.io."
    Both, not either;
(d) its shipped.phext entry is written at migration,
    tending items included, last-tended stamped.
The number is PERMANENT across both registers — migration
never renumbers. Candidates (below) take a number only when
a slot frees: a migration, or Will retiring a moonshot by
ruling.

## Reconciliation — the 'Moonshot 1' of 2026-11-17

On 2026-11-17 Will designated the era-envelope programme
'Moonshot 1' (task 35.6.8/8.7.12/6.5.9). In this register's
from-inception numbering that programme is phccbox, #2;
#1 is phcc, its foundation. The 2026-11-17 label is an alias
for #2 and resolves here — there is no separate moonshot
behind it, and no phantom is created by the old label.

